From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mtbl23 <mtbl23@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 16:20:08 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Leaf port: check the entity type before the distance in
 SetLookAndInteract

Both predicates are pure, so testing the cheap type check first gives the same
result and skips a distance computation for most nearby entities.

Ported from Leaf "Optimize SetLookAndInteract and NearestVisibleLivingEntities" by Taiyou06 <kaandindar21@gmail.com>.
Leaf: https://github.com/Winds-Studio/Leaf

diff --git a/net/minecraft/world/entity/ai/behavior/SetLookAndInteract.java b/net/minecraft/world/entity/ai/behavior/SetLookAndInteract.java
index 71b8f9a7d4fe97f56fe1fc03b48e4dcd455ccd1e..6d2ac04efd0b4cb66547704163925898cb12a47d 100644
--- a/net/minecraft/world/entity/ai/behavior/SetLookAndInteract.java
+++ b/net/minecraft/world/entity/ai/behavior/SetLookAndInteract.java
@@ -20,7 +20,7 @@ public class SetLookAndInteract {
                     i,
                     (lookTarget, interactionTarget, nearestEntities) -> (level, body, timestamp) -> {
                         Optional<LivingEntity> closest = i.<NearestVisibleLivingEntities>get(nearestEntities)
-                            .findClosest(e -> e.distanceToSqr(body) <= interactionRangeSqr && e.is(type));
+                            .findClosest(e -> e.is(type) && e.distanceToSqr(body) <= interactionRangeSqr); // Leaf port - cheaper type check first (Leaf "Optimize SetLookAndInteract and NearestVisibleLivingEntities", Taiyou06); both tests are pure
                         if (closest.isEmpty()) {
                             return false;
                         }
